Rules in force for no-net
File: $T/proj/agent.yaml
Tier: landlock

Can read: Files the agent can open and read.
  Can read any other file on this computer, except the ones under Never reads and Always on.

Can change: Files and folders the agent can create, edit or delete.
  - Can change files in ./out/  [Enforced by the operating system; line 5; editable]
  Cannot change anything else.

Programs: The programs the agent can start.
  - Can run bash  [Enforced by the operating system; line 7; editable]
  - Can run cat  [Enforced by the operating system; line 7; editable]
  Cannot run any other program.

Network: Where the agent can connect.
  Can connect to any address. Other programs' local sockets stay closed (see Always on).

Settings it gets: Environment variables the agent starts with, by name. Values are never shown here.
  - Gets PATH from your shell  [Enforced: other variables are removed before the agent starts; line 9]
  - Gets HOME from your shell  [Enforced: other variables are removed before the agent starts; line 9]
  Every other variable in your shell, secrets included, is removed before it starts.

Limits: When the run is stopped or slowed down.
  No limits of its own: this computer's defaults apply.

Always on: Protections every run gets, written in no rules file.
  - Can never read the usual secret files: SSH and cloud keys, browser profiles, .env files and similar  [Enforced by the operating system; built in]
  - Cannot reach session services, non-SSH credential agents, system D-Bus, X11 or the listed multiplexer and editor sockets; protects their folders from changes  [Best effort: tego refuses it, but a program built to race tego could get past; built in]
  - Cannot reach tego's control sockets or local control ports; its own runtime folder stays available  [Best effort: tego refuses it, but a program built to race tego could get past; built in]
  - Cannot open other terminals; its own terminal and ptys it creates stay available  [Enforced by the operating system and tego; built in]
  - Can never read or change tego's records of its runs  [Enforced by the operating system; built in]
  - Cannot change its own rules file  [Enforced by the operating system; built in]
  - Cannot reach other programs on this computer through their local sockets (Docker, ssh-agent, the desktop bus)  [Best effort: tego refuses it, but a program built to race tego could get past; built in]
  - Can read this computer's network setup: interface names and addresses, routes, and the nearby machines it has talked to  [built in]
  - Cannot gain root through sudo or other setuid programs  [Enforced by the operating system; built in]
  - Writes every refusal and question to a record that cannot be changed unnoticed, and a summary of the rest  [built in]

Rule keys:
  change fs.write fs.write[./out/] enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[bash] enforced (+1 more)
  programs exec.allow exec[cat] enforced
  always-on built-in.deny_read fs.deny_read[$T/home/.ssh] enforced (+1 more)
  always-on builtin.host_ipc builtin.host_ipc best_effort
  always-on builtin.tego_surface builtin.tego_surface best_effort
  always-on builtin.other_tty builtin.other_tty enforced
  always-on built-in.host-sockets host-sockets best_effort
  always-on built-in.route-read route-query none
